Here is a reusable autocomplete input. It filters case-insensitively, hides the menu when there are no matches, validates the current text, supports keyboard selection, and limits the number of rendered suggestions. Filtering may still scan many options when matches are sparse; for very large datasets, use an indexed or server-side search and consider list virtualization.

